    "fb_source_url": "https://facebook.com/100000259835379/posts/pfbid0nTyLG9YPw5WPhEi9VZVbsT7N6P8icjrkL19dXNxUwJxhJTdhEnPjCB2rV3Cke458l/",
    "original_post_text": "No Affidavit. A Business Shut Down. Assets Frozen. Hundreds of Employees Displaced. Is This How Due Process Works?\n\nDoug Polk finally broke his silence on the Lodge Card Club raid and what he revealed should concern every Texas poker player.\n\nThe most important line in his entire statement? That affidavit has not been given to The Lodge or made public.\n\nThe people whose business was shut down don\u2019t even know the specific allegations against them. No arrests. No charges. Just a closed door and hundreds of employees out of work.\n\nA search warrant is not a conviction. But right now it\u2019s being treated like one.\n\nI would love to hear your thoughts and opinions on this ongoing issue. \n\n-ShamGod Poker Report\n\n#TheLodge #DougPolk #PokerNews #TexasPokerRights #PokerCommunity",
    "expanded_title": "No Affidavit. A Business Shut Down. Assets Frozen. Is This How Due Process Works?",
    "expanded_deck": "Doug Polk broke his silence on The Lodge Card Club raid with a detail that should concern every Texas poker player: the search-warrant affidavit still hadn't been given to The Lodge or made public.",
    "expanded_body": "Originally posted March 16, 2026.\n\nNo affidavit. A business shut down. Assets frozen. Hundreds of employees displaced. Is this how due process works?\n\nDoug Polk finally broke his silence on The Lodge Card Club raid, and what he revealed should concern every Texas poker player.\n\nIn his written statement, Polk emphasized that he did not participate in, and had no knowledge of, any money laundering in the operation of The Lodge, while pledging that members with chip balances and tournament payouts would be made whole in coordination with his attorneys.\n\nThe most important line in his entire statement? \"That affidavit has not been given to the Lodge or made public.\"\n\nThe people whose business was shut down didn't even know the specific allegations against them at that point. No arrests. No charges. Just a closed door and hundreds of employees out of work.\n\nA search warrant is not a conviction. But right now it's being treated like one.\n\nI would love to hear your thoughts and opinions on this ongoing issue.\n\n\u2014 Sham",
    "author": "Shomari Williams",
