    "original_post_text": "Thanks to the DFW poker community for keeping me plugged in as this develops. \n\nLodge Card Club Update \u2014 This Just Got Much More Serious\n\nWe now have answers on why TABC raided The Lodge Card Club in Round Rock this past Tuesday \u2014 and it\u2019s bigger than anyone initially assumed.\n\nAccording to a statement from TABC Director of Communications Chris Porter, the agency\u2019s Financial Crimes Unit, along with its Special Investigations Unit and Operations Bureau, executed a search and seizure warrant as part of an ongoing investigation into suspected money laundering and illegal gambling. \n\nEarly speculation centered around liquor licensing issues or underage drinking, which makes sense given TABC\u2019s name. Those assumptions appear to have been incorrect. \n\nApproximately 20 TABC agents were involved in the operation, along with officers from the Williamson County Sheriff\u2019s Office and the IRS.  The IRS being involved is significant, this is now a federal level matter.\n\nNo arrests have been made and no charges have been filed against the business at this time.  The investigation remains ongoing.\n\nThe Lodge remains closed with no reopening timetable announced.\n\nWe will continue to follow this story closely.\n\n#TheLodge #PokerNews #GameIntegrity #TexasPoker\n\nhttps://www.pokernews.com/news/2026/03/lodge-card-club-money-laundering-charges-50804.htm",
    "expanded_title": "Lodge Card Club Update: TABC Financial Crimes and the IRS Were Behind the Raid",
    "expanded_deck": "TABC confirmed its Financial Crimes Unit, the Williamson County Sheriff's Office, and the IRS executed the search warrant at The Lodge over suspected money laundering and illegal gambling \u2014 not a liquor-license check.",
    "expanded_body": "Originally posted March 12, 2026.\n\nThanks to the DFW poker community for keeping me plugged in as this develops.\n\nWe now have answers on why TABC raided The Lodge Card Club in Round Rock on Tuesday, March 10 \u2014 and it's bigger than anyone initially assumed.\n\nAccording to a statement from TABC Director of Communications Chris Porter to PokerNews (https://www.pokernews.com/news/2026/03/lodge-card-club-money-laundering-charges-50804.htm), the agency's Financial Crimes Unit, along with its Special Investigations Unit and Operations Bureau, executed a search and seizure warrant as part of an ongoing investigation into suspected money laundering and illegal gambling.\n\nEarly speculation centered around liquor licensing issues or underage drinking, which makes sense given TABC's name. Those assumptions appear to have been incorrect.\n\nApproximately 20 TABC agents were involved in the operation, along with officers from the Williamson County Sheriff's Office and the IRS. The IRS being involved is significant \u2014 this is a federal-level matter.\n\nNo arrests have been made and no charges have been filed against the business at this time. The investigation remains ongoing, and The Lodge remains closed with no reopening timetable announced.\n\nWe will continue to follow this story closely.\n\n\u2014 Sham",
